WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.629
Despite being the fastest man alive, Barry
Allen a.k.a.

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:08.680
The Flash, played by Grant Gustin, was unable
to outrun the coronavirus in 2020.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.850
Season 6 of the CW series was cut short due
to the cast and crew being unable to finish

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.560
filming the final few episodes, forcing episode
19 to become the makeshift season finale.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:22.520
It functioned as an effective cliffhanger,
considering Iris West mysteriously vanished.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.560
That was back in May of 2020, and fans have
been waiting with bated breath to discover

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.620
her fate.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.289
Fortunately, the season's endgame became a
little clearer with the return of The Flash

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.700
on March 2nd, 2021.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.230
While we've technically now jumped to season
7 of the series, the first episode picks up

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:41.460
right where season 6 episode 19 left off,
so it won't be long until we get the thrilling

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.770
conclusion of Flash going toe-to-toe with
Mirror Master, played by Efrat Dor.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.270
When that battle does commence, however, Team
Flash will be short one member.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:53.600
Season 7 didn't waste any time raising the
stakes, and it did so in a pretty intense

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.530
fashion by offing someone The Flash fans have
been well acquainted with over the last few

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.530
years.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.010
Suffice to say, plenty of viewers were upset
by the death — especially coming on the

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.989
heels of Green Arrow's recent departure from
the franchise he launched.

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:08.479
At least this character said goodbye to The
Flash with a fitting tribute.

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:14.850
“For the flash to run again, Nash Wells
must die.”

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.459
Tom Cavanagh’s character, Harrison Wells,
has gone through an interesting progression

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:20.670
throughout the first six seasons of The Flash.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:25.959
He starts off as your average mentor-turned-villain-in-disguise
before returning to the show via the multiverse.

00:01:25.959 --> 00:01:29.700
Most recently, the Council of Wells found
themselves within the head of the only remaining

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.200
physical version of Wells, who goes by Nash
after the "Crisis on Infinite Earths" event.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.829
In season 7, episode 1, Barry loses his access
to the Speed Force, and the only way he can

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:43.020
get it back is for Nash, and thereby all of
the Harrison Wellses in the multiverse, to

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.020
die.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:50.349
“How can I be the Flash without a Wells
on this team?”

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:54.109
Barry pleads with Nash not to go through with
it, but Nash makes the ultimate sacrifice

00:01:54.109 --> 00:01:57.389
play so that Flash has a chance of stopping
Mirror Master.

00:01:57.389 --> 00:02:01.439
“You’ve Always been the Flash…

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:03.420
You always will be…

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.659
With or with or without me.”

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.700
Cavanagh has been with the series since the
very beginning.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.010
He may have embodied different versions of
the same character, but his presence was practically

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.010
always a given.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:17.900
It looks like that could change for the future
of The Flash, and fans have been pretty emotional

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.200
about the loss.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.540
After all, every version of Wells across every
dimension supposedly died, so it really seems

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.280
like this is the end of his tenure on the
series.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.739
One fan gave the character a proper tribute
by writing,

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:32.180
"For six seasons Tom [Cavanagh] was one of
the best parts of this show.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.590
We will always have the Wells goodbye parade."

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:38.250
Another Twitter user points out that everything
came full circle with his demise:

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.500
"It's funny how a version of Harrison Wells
was responsible for Barry getting his powers

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.250
and now another version of Harrison Wells
made sure that Barry kept his powers."

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.240
Some other comments directed toward Wells
include:

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.670
"I was not prepared for how much of an emotional
roller coaster this episode would be"

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.180
Another user praised Cavanagh, writing:

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:58.099
"Tom Cavanagh as the multiple Harrison Wells
has always been Emmys worthy."

00:02:58.099 --> 00:03:02.230
The Flash just won't be the same without some
version of Harrison Wells around ... so is

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.659
it possible he could come back?

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:06.490
Death is rarely the end in comic book properties.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:11.220
Superman, Batman, and even the other Flash,
Wally West, all bit the dust in the comics

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.040
only to be resurrected shortly thereafter.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.400
Considering multiple versions of Harrison
Wells have already died on the show, it's

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.709
understandable some fans may be suspicious
of the sacrifice.

00:03:20.709 --> 00:03:21.810
One fan speculated,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:25.300
"As much as I feel like they've overplayed
the whole multiple Harrison Wells storyline,

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.599
I don't think they'll just kill him off."

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:31.450
These kinds of fans have good reason not to
feel too down in the dumps yet, as The Flash

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:36.139
showrunner since season 6, Eric Wallace, has
pretty much confirmed actor Tom Cavanagh will

00:03:36.139 --> 00:03:38.401
return in some capacity in the future.

00:03:38.401 --> 00:03:39.610
He told TV Insider,

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:43.379
"Everybody unhappy that their favorite Wells
character or characters is dead, never to

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:47.599
be seen, won't have long to wait because Tom
Cavanagh is still a part of this show."

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:51.700
He goes on to hint how it, quote, "won't take
very long for [his] return in an unexpected

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:52.700
new way."

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.999
There you have it; Harrison Wells isn't gone
for good quite yet.

00:03:55.999 --> 00:03:59.760
It remains to be seen how "unexpected" his
return ends up being.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.770
After all, this is a character we've seen
as a French detective, a cyborg, and a wizard,

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:07.170
so it will take a lot to truly surprise Flash
fans at this point.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:11.499
With the multiverse at its disposal, the show
can be as creative as it needs to be to keep

00:04:11.499 --> 00:04:13.980
an actor as great as Cavanagh onboard.

